{"kind":"issue","id":327,"uid":"01M2PDCNK1VCAKKQZSJF2GS7AV","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","short_id":"s7av","title":"run-170: Dependencies are declared on the plan and installed once at setup, never by a worker — one header line, one setup commit every clone is cut at, and a red on any task that edits a manifest it does not own","body":"**Claim:** do: write the packages a plan needs on one `**Dependencies:**` line and launch it; see: the run installs them once, before any worker starts, as one commit every task is built on and every diff is read against — a task that tries to add a package by editing the manifest itself is stopped on the driver's own pass with a line that says where the package belongs, and a plan with no such line runs exactly as it does today. (elicited)","status":"open","author":"launch","metadata":{"base":"631af3765dd353f1879dd1a8887b130b395467c3","closes":[],"run":170,"target":"popmechanic/ultrapowers"},"revision":1,"created_at":"2026-09-17T00:48:43.105Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T00:48:43.105Z","qualified_id":"popmechanic-ultrapowers#s7av","child_counts":{"open":3,"total":3}}
